{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3067","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3067","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3067\",\"parent_revision\":\"22e5aa78b60a9826d5f9233c0a070236bdc4dec805292741e055f0833f240a49\",\"root_revision\":\"22e5aa78b60a9826d5f9233c0a070236bdc4dec805292741e055f0833f240a49\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] The temp root created by `create_temp_workspace()` is cleaned up (e.g. via `try`/`finally` or a context manager) when the symlink-escape guard rejects a plugin.\\n- [ ] A test proves no temp directory survives a rejected-plugin run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a maintainer, I want `scripts/validate_codex_plugin_isolated.py`'s `create_temp_workspace()` to clean up its `tempfile.mkdtemp()` root when the symlink-escape guard raises `HarnessError`, so rejected plugins don't leak a temp directory on every run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced while fixing PR #2787 deferred finding #7 (issue #3049) \u2014 the new symlink-rejection test confirms the leak: `create_temp_workspace()` creates its temp root via `tempfile.mkdtemp()` *before* the symlink-escape check runs; if that check raises, the directory is never removed. Pre-existing, not introduced by that fix, and out of its 4-finding scope.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ec66225c336bef95a960b46b4c3cfe0d3e820f8706657cf2f1a9e0a40676416b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcUAg\"}"}